1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,552
If your eyelids get heavy twenty minutes after lunch and won't lift till mid-afternoon, look at what's on your desk — the classic American lunch might be the problem.

2
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:22,178
High-glycemic foods spike blood sugar fast, so insulin floods in and can overshoot, crashing sugar below where it started — that crash cuts glucose to your brain and triggers the fatigue.

3
00:00:22,546 --> 00:00:29,846
Fatty foods work differently, linked to a hormone called cholecystokinin that acts on the vagus nerve and brings on sleepiness.

4
00:00:30,214 --> 00:00:32,117
First, the sandwich on white bread.

5
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:40,359
Refined white bread sits around a glycemic index of 75, digesting fast and sending blood sugar up, then crashing hard.

6
00:00:40,727 --> 00:00:42,028
Second, the bag of chips.

7
00:00:42,396 --> 00:00:49,273
Fried and high in fat, linked to that cholecystokinin drowsiness — pairing it with a sugary drink seems to make the dip worse.

8
00:00:49,641 --> 00:00:51,213
Third, the can of soda.

9
00:00:51,581 --> 00:01:00,301
One twelve-ounce can packs about 39 grams of sugar, near ten teaspoons, hitting your bloodstream fast and dropping just as fast.

10
00:01:00,669 --> 00:01:08,998
Swap white bread for whole grain with some turkey, trade chips for a handful of nuts, and pour unsweetened iced tea instead of soda.

11
00:01:09,366 --> 00:01:13,945
One swap at a time makes the afternoon crash easier to handle.
